<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Twentieth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Twentieth Dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Twentieth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> was the last royal dynasty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, ruling in the twelfth and eleventh centuries BCE. Its early king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-iii">Ramesses III</a> repelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-peoples">Sea Peoples</a>, but later reigns saw economic difficulties, tomb robberies and the growing power of the High Priests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amun">Amun</a>. Accounts of the Egyptian Empire New Kingdom treat the dynasty's end with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-xi">Ramesses XI</a> as the close of the New Kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/twentieth-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Twentieth Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Esimpson2 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramesses9.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
